# Public site: no secrets in the repo

This GitHub Pages repo is **public**. Anything committed is world-readable.

## Stay in Make (or officer-typed fields)

- Instagram / Facebook Graph tokens (`EAA…`, `IG…`)
- GitHub PATs
- Compose / update passwords (`COMPOSE_SECRET`, `UPLOAD_SECRET`)
- PhotoPrism **admin** passwords and database credentials

Officers type the compose/update password in the form. Make compares it. Do not hard-code it.

## Allowed in the site

- Make **webhook URLs** already on `/compose/` and `/update/`
- PhotoPrism **album share tokens** in `_data/galleries.yml` (public album links)
- Cheddar Up and Jotform public URLs
- GoatCounter public counter URL

## Do not

- Put tokens, PATs, or passwords in HTML comments, JS, `_config.yml`, or Actions logs.
- Reuse the compose webhook on `/update/` or the Instagram RSS scenario (each Make hook is single-purpose). Form field contracts: `officer-forms.mdc`.
- Change PhotoPrism gallery auth to `Authorization: Bearer` (breaks CORS). Use `POST /api/v1/session` and `X-Session-ID` only.
